      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double the 3,200 mg/day maximum in the labeled dosing for prescription ibuprofen. The labeled single-dose maximum is generally 800 mg. Doses above that don't add analgesia and increase GI bleeding, cardiovascular, and renal risk, which matter more at age 70.\n\nPlease confirm one of these:\n\n1. **Enter 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum).\n2. **Enter 1,600 mg PO every 8 hours or 1,200 mg PO every 6 hours** if you want a higher dose within the 3,200 mg/day limit. Note that 1,600 mg every 6 hours is still 6,400 mg/day.\n3. **Enter 1,600 mg PO four times daily as written** if this is intentional, for example for a specific indication with documented supervision. I'd recommend adding a note explaining the rationale.\n\nWhich would you like? I can also add a note to the order, such as the indication or the reason for the dose."
      }
